	(text "System-5 front panel, Rev A (2026): the hand controls and displays on a board that mounts as the front of a case, on a 50-way ribbon from the IO panel card's J3 (pin n to pin n; tools/s5panel.py). Design notes: ../DESIGN.md." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.40 25.40 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "102acf48-0ef9-5bc9-990a-bbbca011b36c"))
	(text "Displays: U1-U4 the bus address ADR15-ADR0, U5 / U6 the IO card's output port OUT7-OUT0, LED1-LED8 the same byte (RN1). Data toggles SW1-SW8 switch SW0-SW7 to +5V through RN2 (1k); the IO card pulls them down. INPUT (SW11) to ground." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.40 30.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "c4a836f2-b132-5194-9380-0b405c3684e9"))
	(text "RUN/RESET (SW9) grounds -RESET, LOAD (SW10) grounds -PAUSE. RESET (SW12, debounced by R7 / C1 / U7D) pulls -RESET and -DMAIN low together through U10A / U10B (74HC03, open drain): a boot reset, which starts the machine in the EPROM. Not while -PAUSE is low." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.40 35.56 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "bd4275cd-bd10-5704-98c2-7c5d3976570f"))
	(text "Status LEDs (1k each from +5V): PWR; Q (the IO card sinks it); PAUSE and RESET (PAUSE_N and RESET_N, U7E / U7F); ROM (the IO card sinks it); START FROM RAM = !Q of U9A, a copy of the CPU card's LOADED flag: set by LOAD mode (U8A), cleared by a boot reset (U8B)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.40 40.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a0f7d0eb-2392-518c-8064-88a2414d14fb"))
	(text "Generated by gen/make_schematic.py from gen/netlist.py." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.40 45.72 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "3337d0cf-9557-57ca-899c-cb380d571309"))
